# aurora.local / packages/photos/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/photos/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/photos/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# DIFFERENT FROM EVERY OTHER FILE IN THIS SET: two of this package's four
# images (immich-server, immich-machine-learning) are ALREADY
# parameterised via `${IMMICH_VERSION:-release}` in compose.yml, and
# IMMICH_VERSION already exists in packages/photos/.env.example. That
# means pinning them does not need `scripts/pin.sh --apply` at all —
# render_pins() sources this file into the environment before
# `docker compose up`, and IMMICH_VERSION is a normal compose
# interpolation variable, so setting it here takes effect immediately,
# with no compose.yml rewrite required. Recorded as IMMICH_VERSION below,
# not as IMAGE_IMMICH_SERVER/IMAGE_IMMICH_ML.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, the two IMAGE_* entries below are consumed
# the same way as every other package: sourced by render_pins() but only
# wired into compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply` has
# rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — not done here. compose.yml is
# untouched by this work either way.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# IMMICH_VERSION — Immich has no LTS branch; its own docs say to expect
# breaking changes between releases and to read release notes and back
# up the database and library before every upgrade. Pinned to v3.1.0
# (2026-07-27, ~19 days before this check, stable). immich-server and
# immich-machine-learning MUST use the exact same version — that
# constraint is enforced here by both images below being verified
# against the same v3.1.0 tag. Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 —
# confirmed for both images. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMMICH_VERSION=v3.1.0
# For reference/provenance (not consumed unless scripts/pin.sh --apply
# is run and compose.yml is changed to use ${IMAGE_<SVC>} instead of
# ${IMMICH_VERSION}):
IMAGE_IMMICH_SERVER=ghcr.io/immich-app/immich-server:v3.1.0@sha256:b434cb9287eea1471c9974845914d4dd328c9c2d652e446ed4930f99944f0ceb
IMAGE_IMMICH_ML=ghcr.io/immich-app/immich-machine-learning:v3.1.0@sha256:5a0839dc5303cd7215bcd2180a26aed3af41675aefb3e75e5157e9f10ad16e6e

# docker.io/redis (immich-redis) — FINDING: Redis 6 reached end of life
# on 2025-08-31 and receives no further upstream fixes; Immich's own
# current docker-compose template has moved to `valkey/valkey:8`
# instead of Redis entirely. compose.yml still uses `redis:6.2-alpine`,
# which currently resolves to patch 6.2.23-alpine (still getting Alpine
# base-image security rebuilds, but the Redis 6 codebase itself is
# frozen upstream). Recorded below is that current patch — a digest
# freeze of a dead line, not a "safe" pin in the way the rest of this
# file is. For reference (NOT adopted — different image, out of scope
# for this task, and a real migration: Immich would need its Redis/
# Valkey connection config checked, not just an image swap):
#   valkey/valkey:8@sha256:495e4fecdc98ee48a20b207726caa5ab6451e0fac3642a9be10d9e70b3068df6
# Multi-arch on redis:6.2.23-alpine: linux/386, linux/amd64,
# linux/arm/v6, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64/v8, linux/ppc64le,
# linux/riscv64, linux/s390x — confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_IMMICH_REDIS=redis:6.2.23-alpine@sha256:ec5e187c913d422cdf60f4216a5fdfb95246792c6de6fe21ff5bed75cbfc8c23

# docker.io/tensorchord/pgvecto-rs (immich-postgres) — FINDING: this is
# EXACTLY the image Immich's own upgrade docs say to migrate away from.
# pgvecto-rs is deprecated in favour of VectorChord; the docs give the
# precise replacement for our exact tag: `pg14-v0.2.0` ->
# `ghcr.io/immich-app/postgres:14-vectorchord0.4.3-pgvectors0.2.0`.
# This is a real database-engine migration (back up first — Immich's
# own docs and community reports describe cases where it did not go
# smoothly), not a version bump, so it is deliberately NOT adopted here.
# Recorded below is a digest freeze of the current, deprecated
# `pg14-v0.2.0` (matches what compose.yml already runs), plus the
# documented replacement for reference:
#   ghcr.io/immich-app/postgres:14-vectorchord0.4.3-pgvectors0.2.0@sha256:bcf63357191b76a916ae5eb93464d65c07511da41e3bf7a8416db519b40b1c23
# Multi-arch on both: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 — confirmed. Checked
# 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_IMMICH_POSTGRES=docker.io/tensorchord/pgvecto-rs:pg14-v0.2.0@sha256:739cdd626151ff1f796dc95a6591b55a714f341c737e27f045019ceabf8e8c52
